---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
export const title = "Trying to cry is also a distraction";
export const bookTitle = "Likutay Aitzos";
---
<Layout title="{title} - {bookTitle}" description="{title} from {bookTitle} - Hisbodidus teachings from Rebbe Nachman">
  <div class="book-page">
    <header class="book-header">
      <h1>{bookTitle}</h1>
      <h2>Section 15: {title}</h2>
    </header>
    <nav class="chapter-nav">
  <a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch14" class="nav-btn prev">← Previous</a>
  <a href="/books/likutay-aitzos" class="nav-btn main">Main</a>
  <a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch16" class="nav-btn next">Next →</a>
</nav>
    <article class="chapter-content">
      <h3 class="chapter-title">{title}</h3>
      <p class="book-para">Even though crying before Hashem Yisburach with entreaties and beseeching is extremely good, even still, when a person says Psalms or other entreaties and supplications, or converses personally with his Creator, and he thinks and anticipates, and looks mindfully all the time that he should cry and shed tears, this also is a (distracting) foreign thought, and confuses the kavana (-concentration, intention). Because the main thing is – that he should concentrate his mind to say the words truly with all his heart, that he should incline his ear and his heart to hear what he is expressing with his mouth, and if he is aroused to cry, how wonderful – and if not, he should not confuse his concentrations for this.</p>
<p class="book-para">Na Nach Nachma Nachman MayUman</p><p class="source-ref">(Likutay Moharan II, Torah 95; Outpouring of the Soul 3)</p>
    </article>
    <nav class="chapter-nav">
  <a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch14" class="nav-btn prev">← Previous</a>
  <a href="/books/likutay-aitzos" class="nav-btn main">Main</a>
  <a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch16" class="nav-btn next">Next →</a>
</nav>
    <footer class="book-footer">
      <a href="/books/likutay-aitzos" class="back-link">← Back to Table of Contents</a>
    </footer>
  </div>
</Layout>
<style>
  .book-page { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1rem; }
  .book-header { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2rem; padding-bottom: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 2px solid #e2e8f0; }
  .book-header h1 { font-size: 1.5rem; color: #1a365d; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .book-header h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; color: #4a5568; margin: 0; font-weight: 500; }
  .chapter-nav { display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 1rem; margin: 1.5rem 0; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .nav-btn { display: inline-block; padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem; background: #1a365d; color: white; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 500; transition: all 0.2s; }
  .nav-btn:hover { background: #2d4a6f; transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .nav-btn.disabled { background: #cbd5e0; cursor: not-allowed; }
  .nav-btn.main { background: #059669; }
  .nav-btn.main:hover { background: #047857; }
  .chapter-content { background: white; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); line-height: 1.8; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .chapter-title { font-size: 1.5rem; color: #1a365d; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding-bottom: 0.75rem; border-bottom: 2px solid #e2e8f0; }
  .book-para { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; text-align: justify; color: #2d3748; }
  .source-ref { font-style: italic; color: #718096; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: 1rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px dashed #e2e8f0; }
  .book-footer { text-align: center; margin-top: 2rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 2px solid #e2e8f0; }
  .back-link { color: #1a365d; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 500; }
  .back-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .chapter-content { padding: 1.5rem; font-size: 1rem; } .chapter-nav { gap: 0.5rem; } .nav-btn { padding: 0.6rem 1rem; font-size: 0.9rem; } }
</style>
